{"id": "6b8ddec4-c364-478b-9e8d-250c82562e8f", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Based on AWS Elemental MediaTailor documentation:

**What happens when exceeded:** `PersonalizationThresholdSeconds` defines the maximum duration of underfilled ad time (in seconds) allowed in an ad break. If the unfilled ad time exceeds this threshold, MediaTailor **abandons personalization of the ad break** and instead shows the **underlying content** in its place.

**Precondition for the threshold to apply:** This only works for **ad replacement** (in live or VOD streams) — not ad insertion — because the fallback relies on there being an underlying content stream to fall back to. If there's no underlying content (pure ad insertion), there's nothing to revert to, so the threshold has no effect in that case.", "type": "text"}], "created_at": null}

{"id": "39938e34-07ae-42cd-b855-666d2e3bd7f0", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Based on AWS Elemental MediaTailor documentation:

**What happens when exceeded:** `PersonalizationThresholdSeconds` defines the maximum duration of underfilled ad time (in seconds) allowed in an ad break. If the unfilled ad time exceeds this threshold, MediaTailor **abandons personalization of the ad break** and instead shows the **underlying content** in its place.

**Precondition for the threshold to apply:** This only works for **ad replacement** (in live or VOD streams) — not ad insertion — because the fallback relies on there being an underlying content stream to fall back to. If there's no underlying content (pure ad insertion), there's nothing to revert to, so the threshold has no effect in that case."}]}
